## 7. Mapping Registry Data Structure

Design a logical registry containing the following fields:

| Field | Purpose |
|---|---|
| mapping_id | Unique mapping record identifier |
| mapping_version | Mapping configuration version |
| category_id | Existing business category identifier |
| category_name | Verified category name |
| agent_id | Primary agent identifier |
| agent_name | Agent display name |
| mapping_type | Primary |
| mapping_status | Draft, Under Review, Approved, Active, Deprecated |
| category_scope | Business category boundaries |
| supported_workflows | Authorized workflow references |
| required_context | Required category context |
| shared_dependencies | Shared service dependencies |
| restrictions | Agent restrictions |
| created_at | Registry creation timestamp |
| updated_at | Last update timestamp |
| approved_by | Authorized approval reference |
| approval_timestamp | Approval timestamp |

This is a logical design only. Do not create a database table or collection during this step.

